---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocMock from '../../../components/DocMock.astro';

const headings = [
  { id: 'before-you-write', text: 'Before you write' },
  { id: 'what-to-include',  text: 'What to include' },
  { id: 'how-to-send',      text: 'Generating and sending a report' },
  { id: 'response-times',   text: 'Response times' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Contact Support"
  description="How to write an effective BudgetBaby support request, what to include, how to send a diagnostics report, and expected response times."
  canonical="/budgetbaby/docs/contact-support"
  headings={headings}
>
  <div class="docs-content">
    <h1>Contact Support</h1>
    <p class="docs-summary">
      Our support team reads every email personally. Including the right information up front
      means we can usually resolve your issue in one reply instead of several back-and-forth messages.
    </p>

    <h2 id="before-you-write">Before you write</h2>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Self-serve checks" caption="Three minutes of pre-flight resolves most issues without an email.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span></span><span class="dm-bar-title">Before contacting</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">1</span><span class="dm-row-label">Force-quit & reopen<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">App switcher</div></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">2</span><span class="dm-row-label">Update the app<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">App Store · pull to refresh</div></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">3</span><span class="dm-row-label">iOS 17.0 or later<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Settings → General</div></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">4</span><span class="dm-row-label">Search Troubleshooting<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">/budgetbaby/docs</div></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">5</span><span class="dm-row-label">Restore Purchases<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Settings → Premium Features</div></span></div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>
    <p>Most issues are resolved without needing to contact support. Please try these first:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Force-quit and reopen the app.</strong> Swipe up from the Home bar to open the app switcher, swipe BudgetBaby off the screen, then reopen it.</li>
      <li><strong>Update the app.</strong> Open the App Store, tap your profile, and pull to refresh. Many reported issues are fixed in the latest version.</li>
      <li><strong>Check your iOS version.</strong> BudgetBaby requires iOS 17.0 or later. Settings → General → About shows your current version.</li>
      <li><strong>Search this documentation.</strong> The <a href="/budgetbaby/docs/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a> page covers the most common issues with step-by-step solutions.</li>
      <li><strong>Restore Premium.</strong> If Premium features are not showing, try Settings → Premium Features → Restore Purchases before writing to us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="what-to-include">What to include</h2>
    <p>
      The more context you provide, the faster we can help. Please include all of the following
      when you write:
    </p>
    <div class="doc-formula">
Subject: [Brief description of your issue]

App version: (Settings → About → Version number)
iOS version: (Settings → General → About → iOS Version)
Device: (iPhone model, e.g. iPhone 15 Pro)
Account type: (free / Premium / not signed in)

What happened:
[Describe what you did and what you expected to happen]

What you see instead:
[Describe the unexpected behavior, error message, or symptom]

Steps to reproduce:
1.
2.
3.

Screenshots or screen recording: (attached / not available)
Support report attached: (yes — see below / no)
    </div>
    <div class="doc-tip">
      <strong>Data loss issues.</strong> If you believe you have lost transactions or budget data, contact us before uninstalling or resetting the app. Include your app version and iOS version. We flag data loss reports for same-day triage and may be able to help recover data.
    </div>

    <h2 id="how-to-send">Generating and sending a report</h2>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Pre-filled email" caption="The Mail share-sheet route includes the BB-XXXX-XXXX code automatically.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Cancel</span><span class="dm-bar-title">New Message</span><span class="dm-bar-action">Send</span></div>
        <div class="dm-card" style="padding:8px 9px; gap:3px;">
          <div class="dm-kv"><span class="muted">To:</span><strong>support@babyblocks.io</strong></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span class="muted">From:</span><span class="muted">insightintriguing@…</span></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span class="muted">Subject:</span><strong>[BB-9F3K-2A17] Bills not appearing</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card" style="padding:8px 9px; min-height:60px;">
          <div class="dm-help" style="font-size:8.5px; color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.4;">App version: 2.1.3 (412)<br/>iOS version: 17.4.1<br/>Device: iPhone 15 Pro<br/>Account: Premium<br/><br/>What happened…</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon upload" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#475569,#1e293b);">A</span><span class="dm-row-label">BudgetBaby_Diagnostics_…<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">512 KB · attached</div></span></div>
      </DocMock>
      <DocMock label="Report archive" caption="Every report is kept for 90 days under Settings → Support.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Support</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Archive</span><span class="dm-bar-action">⋯</span></div>
        <div class="dm-section-label">Recent reports</div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">B</span><span class="dm-row-label">BB-9F3K-2A17<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Mar 01, 14:35 · Bills</div></span><span class="dm-row-chevron"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">B</span><span class="dm-row-label">BB-7B2L-9C04<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Feb 24, 09:12 · Backup</div></span><span class="dm-row-chevron"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">B</span><span class="dm-row-label">BB-3A8X-1F66<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Feb 11, 18:48 · Premium</div></span><span class="dm-row-chevron"></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-help">Tap any to re-share without regenerating.</div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>
    <p>
      For most issues, attaching a support report dramatically reduces resolution time.
      The report contains no financial data — only app-state metadata and anonymous event logs.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to <strong>Settings → Support and Diagnostics</strong>.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Report a Problem</strong> and follow the 5-step guided flow, or tap <strong>Export Diagnostics</strong> for an immediate capture.</li>
      <li>When prompted, choose <strong>Mail</strong> from the share sheet. BudgetBaby pre-fills the subject line with your support code (<code>BB-XXXX-XXXX</code>) and attaches the report.</li>
      <li>Add your description and send to <a href="mailto:support@babyblocks.io">support@babyblocks.io</a>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      If you do not have Mail configured, use AirDrop to transfer the file to your Mac and
      attach it manually to your email, or use <strong>Copy Support Report</strong> to paste
      a plain-text version inline.
    </p>
    <p>
      All generated reports are saved to the archive at Settings → Support and Diagnostics → View Archive
      for 90 days. You can re-share any archived report without regenerating it.
    </p>
    <p>
      For a detailed explanation of what is included in the report, see
      <a href="/budgetbaby/docs/troubleshooting#diagnostics">Generating a support report</a>
      in the Troubleshooting guide.
    </p>

    <h2 id="response-times">Response times</h2>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Triage tiers" caption="Data-loss reports are flagged for same-day triage.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span></span><span class="dm-bar-title">Response times</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Standard</strong><span class="dm-pill green">1–2 business days</span></div>
          <div class="dm-help">Bug reports, billing questions, how-tos.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-warn">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Data loss</strong><span class="dm-pill orange">Same day</span></div>
          <div class="dm-help" style="color:#FDBA74;">Flagged on intake. Don't uninstall before you hear back.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-accent">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Security</strong><span class="dm-pill purple">2 business days</span></div>
          <div class="dm-help">Use [Security] in the subject line.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv muted"><span>Channel</span><strong>Email only</strong></div>
          <div class="dm-kv muted"><span>Read by</span><strong>A human</strong></div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Standard issues:</strong> Reply within 1-2 business days.</li>
      <li><strong>Data loss or corruption:</strong> Flagged for same-day triage. Reply within a few hours during business hours.</li>
      <li><strong>Security reports:</strong> Acknowledgment within 2 business days. Use <strong>[Security]</strong> in the subject line. See the <a href="/security">Security page</a> for our full disclosure policy.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We are a small team. We do not have a live chat or phone line. Email is the only support channel,
      and we commit to reading every message personally.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Support email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@babyblocks.io">support@babyblocks.io</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
